Background: Stroke is clinically diagnosed as an acute, localized neurological impairment that is caused by vascular damage (infarction, hemorrhage) to the central nervous system. This main leading cause of demise and dysfunction worldwide resulting in frequent deficit, hemiplegia, which briefly affects upper limb. This multicentered study is the first to provide updated normative reference values for FMA-UE in post stroke adults in wide range of age in Pakistan’s population.&#x0D;
Objective: To determine Pakistani normative values of Fugl-Meyer Assessment on upper extremity in post Stroke Population.&#x0D;
Methods: Descriptive cross-sectional study on 1260 post-stroke patients was conducted in various public and private physiotherapy centers of country using Fugl-Meyer Assessment (Upper-Extremity) FMA-UE scale after ethical approval. Hemiplegic survivors of both genders aged 45-75 years were taken using convenience sampling technique, informed consent was taken. Statistics was done using SPSS version25.&#x0D;
